Rodin Essential is the native hardware-control suite for the Xiaomi Rodin
(POCO X7 Pro / Redmi Turbo 4, MediaTek MT6899) written and maintained by
NEESCHAL-3. The upstream project, its licence and its notices are preserved
in this repository; see LICENSE for the Apache License, Version 2.0 and
CHANGELOG.md for the upstream release history.

This repository reworks that project for the MediaTek MT6991 `dash` platform
(POCO X8 Pro Max / REDMI Turbo 5 Max) by afrizal1211, along the SaanOS line
of the same project by Saan. The port is tested on real hardware by the
@PocoX8ProMaxID Telegram community. The upstream release this port is based
on is v1.18.5. The application package was renamed from
`io.github.neeschal.rodinessential` to `io.github.neeschal.dashessential`,
the root module id from `nees_rodin_essential_backend` to
`nees_dash_essential_backend`, and the SELinux types, classes and helper names
were moved into the `dash_*` namespace.

What the port changed:

  * The GPU actuation model. The upstream target published a uniformly spaced
    26 MHz operating-point ladder, so an OPP index could be computed from a
    frequency. Dash's ladder is not uniformly spaced and the GPUEB's index
    space does not match the Mali devfreq table's, so every operating-point
    index is now resolved against the ladder the driver publishes at
    /proc/gpufreqv2/gpu_working_opp_table. A request the ladder cannot satisfy
    is an error rather than a guessed index.

  * The GPU device addresses and frequency ladder. Dash carries the Arm
    Immortalis-G925 at mali@48000000 with a 338 MHz to 1612 MHz ladder, against
    the upstream target's 13000000.mali and 260 MHz to 1300 MHz ladder. The
    Mali cooling device is now resolved by its type rather than by a fixed
    cooling_device index.

  * The CPU, UFS, DVFSRC, backlight, touch panel and display baselines, all
    retargeted to the values the shipped dash kernel, device tree and ROM
    report.

  * The SELinux genfs rules for the Mali devfreq, UFS devfreq and DVFSRC
    devfreq nodes.

